phases[12]{phase,feature,state}:
  1,watertight-mesh import gate + caustics on loaded meshes,done
  2,path tracer core (NEE+MIS+RR) + procedural sky (Preetham/Perez),done
  3,GLB loading + Gaussian-splat (.ply) import,done
  4,mesh -> sparse voxel grid (MATERIAL_VOXEL),done
  5,mesh -> dense signed distance field (MATERIAL_SDF),done
  6,HDRI/environment lighting + importance sampling,done
  7,caustics via progressive photon map,done
  8,selectable tonemap operator (AgX default),done
  9,live ImGui controls replacing CLI-only workflow,done
  10,OptiX AI denoiser (color-only),done
  11,NanoVDB volumetric medium (MATERIAL_NVDB) — Woodcock tracking + HG phase,done
  12,spatial RIS for surface NEE (RTXDI idea, not the SDK) — reservoirNEE toggle,done

notes[13]{note}:
  "Review-pass fixes on the hybrid SDF glass push, found by actually rendering each scene, not just reading code: emitFromSun was missing a /pdfDir term (light-subpath vs eye-side NEE estimator mismatch), and default sun angular-radius/intensity were too physically-tiny/dim to matter once correctly Ω-scaled — together these made the glass cup's caustic render completely flat. Fixed + retuned (2.0deg/10000 defaults); caustic now shows real structure. Also: SceneSource::emptyBase fixed the material probe scene silently rendering on top of the bring-up scene's spheres (extraSdf-only content fell through to buildFixedTestScene()); ProjectBakeState::haveSdf/haveVoxels (transient, broke a live partial-rebuild path) replaced by deriving the same condition from state.representation/haveMesh directly."
  "scripts/gen_filemap.py is plain Python over src/tests/, no CMake/build dependency — run standalone anytime via `python3 scripts/gen_filemap.py` (docs/agent/commands.toon's filemap table) for a fast file-map/seam-violation check mid-iteration; the agent_filemap CMake target (moved to the top of CMakeLists.txt, right after find_package(OpenGL)) runs the identical script as an ALL step so a built tree also never goes stale."
  "Hybrid SDF glass push: dielectric SDF materials (SdfGrid::branch/palette, bakeAnalyticSdfPalette), nested glass/liquid IOR resolved by same-grid ray-relative branch lookup (no medium stack), __intersection__sdf rewritten to sphere-trace correctly from inside a dielectric, light subpaths now run through MATERIAL_SDF (real caustics through the glass cup, verified by render). New analytic SunLight (Params::sun), MIS-mixed 50/50 with env/quad NEE and light-subpath emission; solid Params::backgroundColor on primary-ray misses only (HDRI still visible through glass/reflections). makeGlassCupSdf + makeMaterialProbeSdfs are the two new procedural scenes."
  "Project window gates startup: main() opens Project only (Viewport/Settings not constructed until a scene is Baked). Hidden 1x1 GLFW anchor window shares GL context to all three panel AppWindows so any panel can close/reopen independently (OS close and the checkbox row both durably close now). rebuildScene() split into 5 phases (load/classify/representation/environment/construct-renderer) advanced one per frame by the Project window, logged to an on-screen bakeLog + stderr. 3-entry SceneDescriptor registry, all three real: Bring-up scene, Material probe (9-sphere roughness/IOR sweep), Glass cup (the north star). Changing procedural-sky sliders or the sun toggle live-rebuilds the environment + renderer (rebuildEnvironmentLive) instead of a no-op resetAccumulation."
  "ITALY_SCENE=<registry index> selects which scene the ITALY_DUMP_FRAME headless hook bakes (default 0, Bring-up)."
  "All 10 planned MVP phases done as of the correctness+doctrine pass; see humans.md Status for full narrative/war-stories per phase."
  "Content pivot (post-MVP): hybrid SDF+gsplat procedural rendering is now the active direction, not deferred. GLB import gated to box/sphere/cylinder prims via io/mesh_primitive_classify (analytic PCA shape-fit); assets/test.glb is now rejected by that gate. Procedural SDF authoring: convert/sdf_primitives.h + bakeAnalyticSdf. SceneSource::extraSdf is a vector; light subpaths refuse to run on voxel/gsplat scenes (SBT guard) but are now allowed for dielectric SDF."
  "Since MVP: VCM merge-term moved to a GAS spatial query (ALLOW_SINGLE_GAS flag fix, light-leak fix, maxConnectionsPerVertex=128, ~12.5x); --cup procedural CSG bowl via extraSdf."
  "Deferred, not forgotten: voxel-as-SDF-accelerator/detail-modulator/storage, gsplat fine detail inside the voxel volume, participating-medium liquid, scanned/photogrammetry ingestion, SDF animation/deformation, gsplat<->SDF attachment transforms, mesh->3DGS fitting, full VCM/ReSTIR caustics, per-kind light-subpath hit-groups, capsule/cone prim kinds, Metal backend."
  "NanoVDB volumetric medium (Phase 2 of a separate rendering-tech plan, not the original MVP's phase list): GeometryKind::Nvdb + __intersection__nvdb report an AABB entry/exit interval; MATERIAL_NVDB branch in __closesthit__radiance does real Woodcock/delta-tracking multi-scatter (global-max-density majorant, see humans.md claudia marker) with Henyey-Greenstein phase sampling and NEE against sun/env/quad light; shadow rays through the medium use ratio-tracking transmittance (mediumTransmittance), also applied to surface NEE so light reaching non-volume geometry through fog attenuates correctly. src/io/nvdb_loader.h/.cpp synthesizes a procedural fog-sphere FloatGrid on the host (nanovdb::tools::createFogVolumeSphere) with no CUDA/OptiX includes (seam rule); optix_renderer.cpp uploads the raw grid blob and reinterpret_casts it on device. NanoVDB pulled via FetchContent from the openvdb repo (nanovdb/ subtree only, via FetchContent_Populate not MakeAvailable — avoids configuring OpenVDB's own heavy CMakeLists) at tag v12.1.1 (v12.0.0 has a real GCC template-lookup compile bug in tools/GridBuilder.h, fixed upstream by v12.1.1). --fog CLI flag + ImGui sliders (radius/voxel size/sigma_t/albedo/g/density) in src/app/main.cpp; light subpaths (VCM) disabled when an Nvdb object is present, same guard as Voxel/Gsplat. Verified by rendering the fog sphere over the bring-up scene at sigma_t~=0 vs sigma_t=8 and eyeballing the PNG diff (ITALY_NVDB_SIGMA_T)."
  "Phase 3 of a separate rendering-tech plan (RTXDI-idea spatial RIS, not the SDK — see humans.md realism/claudia markers): __raygen__reservoirBuild draws 6 candidate light samples (sun/env/quad) per pixel per subframe into Params::reservoirBuffer, then the main pass's primary-hit (depth==0) surface NEE mixes in 4 spatial-neighbor reservoirs via weighted-reservoir-sampling before consuming the winning sample through the existing traceOcclusion/mediumTransmittance/BSDF path unchanged. No temporal reservoir carry-over across subframes (would double-count against accumBuffer). Volume NEE is out of scope this phase (Woodcock-tracked scatter position isn't stable enough between build/main passes for reservoir reuse); RenderSettings::reservoirNEE (default off, ITALY_RESERVOIR_NEE) and extraTestLightCount (ITALY_TEST_EXTRA_LIGHTS, up to 3 virtual NEE-only quad lights with no geometry) gate/support it. Verified: single-quad-light scene shows matching global mean off vs on (no bias regression), many-light scene shows ~16% lower local-gradient noise proxy at 8 subframes with RIS on, and matching global means at 128-subframe convergence (unbiased). A first implementation divided RIS candidate weights by the light's area-measure pdf while the target function was solid-angle-measure (missing the dist^2/cosTheta Jacobian) — silently biased brighter by ~10%; caught by comparing global mean pixel value before/after, not just eyeballing, and fixed by dividing by the Jacobian-converted solid-angle pdf throughout."
  "Phase 4 of the same rendering-tech plan (RTXGI/NRD/DLSS evaluation) shipped no code — see humans.md realism/claudia markers. Verdict: RTXGI and NRD scoped out fully (both solve real-time-with-motion-history problems italy doesn't have; italy's converged-progressive/static-camera model is already served correctly by direct unbiased GI and the Phase-1 OptiX AI Denoiser). DLSS Frame Generation scoped out, no exception (no frame-rate target to smooth toward). DLSS Super-Resolution is the one plausible fit (navigation-preview upscaling) but deferred, not implemented, pending evidence that native-res preview is actually slow."
  "This file is hand-maintained: update it when humans.md's ## Status section changes. Source of truth is humans.md prose; this is the compact index."
